WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.770
- I love how open you
are about mental health

00:00:02.770 --> 00:00:04.710
because I have similar issues

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:05.930
and I've suffered from depression.

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:07.440
And I think a lot of people,

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:10.160
especially in the creative
world or just from childhood,

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:11.960
you've been kind of trained to

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:14.030
just keep going and you can handle it,

00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:15.937
and especially as a woman, it's like,

00:00:15.937 --> 00:00:18.410
"Don't let them see you
sweat," like, you know?

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:20.930
So I just love that you're open about that

00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:25.810
because not everybody's as
vulnerable at being like that,

00:00:25.810 --> 00:00:28.290
and I think it's helpful for your fans.

00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:29.780
'Cause I know in every meet and greet

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:31.440
you probably get people
saying that, I do too,

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:33.027
and they're like, "Man, thank you for just

00:00:33.027 --> 00:00:35.407
"being open in your
songs and open, you know,

00:00:35.407 --> 00:00:37.957
"with everybody 'cause I
felt like this was just me,

00:00:37.957 --> 00:00:40.127
"and knowing that somebody
else is going through it

00:00:40.127 --> 00:00:43.080
"makes you not feel alone
and so depressed about it."

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:44.590
So thank you for doing that.

00:00:44.590 --> 00:00:45.830
It's really hard.

00:00:45.830 --> 00:00:50.830
- I just have to say that
you were the first idol

00:00:51.140 --> 00:00:53.438
that I ever had and-

00:00:53.438 --> 00:00:54.380
- You are so sweet.

00:00:54.380 --> 00:00:58.470
- I wouldn't be the artist,
or even the person, that I am

00:00:58.470 --> 00:01:02.270
with being so outspoken,
and vulnerable, and fearless

00:01:02.270 --> 00:01:03.930
if I hadn't had you to look up to.

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:05.880
So I thank you for that because-

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:07.080
- Well you're very nice.

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:12.080
- Yes, I just like, I looked
at you as my idol growing up.

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:18.350
You are fearless, and
courageous, and real as-

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:20.664
You know?

00:01:20.664 --> 00:01:21.497
- Yep.

00:01:21.497 --> 00:01:22.750
- And I love that about you,

00:01:22.750 --> 00:01:25.250
and I've always just thought to myself,

00:01:25.250 --> 00:01:26.487
when I was younger I
always thought to myself,

00:01:26.487 --> 00:01:28.707
"If I ever make it I wanna be like her,

00:01:28.707 --> 00:01:32.029
"because she's real,
and she's genuine," and-

00:01:32.029 --> 00:01:33.580
- Well, and I think the
thing about it, though,

00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:35.377
is even you're saying like, you know,

00:01:35.377 --> 00:01:37.100
"You're strong, you're courageous,
you're all those things,"

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:38.130
I'm not all the time!

00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:39.515
It takes work.

00:01:39.515 --> 00:01:41.710
That's the thing I think
everybody looks at us

00:01:41.710 --> 00:01:44.967
as like even when you overcome
something they're like,

00:01:44.967 --> 00:01:46.120
"Okay, she's already overcome that."

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:47.877
I'm like, "No, no, no,
that's a daily effort

00:01:47.877 --> 00:01:49.360
"in trying to be positive."

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:52.440
That's a daily effort
and that's not a given,

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:53.710
like you're just over it and you went

00:01:53.710 --> 00:01:55.220
to some magical therapy session

00:01:55.220 --> 00:01:56.530
and it's over.
- Right.

00:01:56.530 --> 00:01:59.440
I think that that's a daily
thing that you work at,

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:02.080
and a daily thing that I
work at, and I don't know.

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:04.390
Thank you for the compliments,
but I just think it's really,

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:05.370
it's a really cool thing,

00:02:05.370 --> 00:02:08.000
and it's not easy to always
have a spotlight on you

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:09.550
and arrows being aimed at you,

00:02:09.550 --> 00:02:11.440
especially when you are vulnerable

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:15.000
and you give people more ammo
for all the trolls out there.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:17.700
So, anyway, but thank you for doing that.

